e chicken in a large bowl. Mix the marinade ingredients in a separate bowl.","Pour the marinade over the chicken and turn to coat. Cover and refrigerate overnight.","Preheat the oven to 180°C/350°F. Line a roasting tin with foil.","Lift the chicken out of the marinade and arrange it in the tin. Reserve the excess marinade for basting.","Roast for 45 minutes, or until cooked through. Turn the chicken and baste halfway through cooking. Any marinade used for basting must cook thoroughly with the chicken. Discard any unused raw marinade.","Serving suggestion: serve with steamed rice and salad.","See Cooking and storage for cooling, storing and reheating leftovers."],"prepMinutes":null,"cookMinutes":null,"waitMinutes":null,"timeNote":"The book does not give separate total preparation, cooking and waiting times. Follow the timings stated in each method step.","notes":"","allergens":[],"allergenNote":"Allergens have not been independently classified. Check every ingredient label, including alternatives, sauces and protein powders.","sourceWarnings":[],"version":2},{"id":"turkish-lamb-chops","name":"Turkish lamb chops","category":"Dinner","servings":4,"servingLabel":"lamb chop","servingBasis":"Makes 4 lamb chops / per lamb chop","nutrition":{"protein":18,"calories":287,"carbs":2,"fat":23},"nutritionSource":"The High Protein Kitchen, page 87. Values reproduced from the uploaded book; supplied estimates, not independently analysed. Brands, alternatives and optional ingredients can change the figures.","nutritionStatus":"source-estimate","source":"The High Protein Kitchen · p. 87","sourceBook":"high-protein-kitchen","sourceRecipeNumber":58,"sourcePage":87,"sourceImagePage":86,"sourceSha256":"0d37a347d76583ab9cf99ea56ee38cabb98021b5f7f7019f0e1eb070f01f88a3","image":"/assets/cookbook/recipe-058.webp","imageNote":"Original recipe photograph supplied in The High Protein Kitchen, page 86.","quote":"A short rest before serving. For the lamb, unfortunately.","ingredients":[{"name":"4 x bone-in lamb chops (approx 140g /5 oz each)","quantity":null,"unit":"","note":"Quantity as printed; choose an explicit amount in your own version to scale numerically.","group":"Main","optional":false,"aisle":"Other","sourceText":"4 x bone-in lamb chops (approx 140g /5 oz each)","sourceQuantity":null,"sourceUnit":"","alternateMeasure":"","scalingMode":"compound"},{"name":"avocado oil or butter","quantity":2,"unit":"tsps","note":"","group":"Main","optional":false,"aisle":"Other","sourceText":"2 tsps avocado oil or butter","sourceQuantity":2,"sourceUnit":"tsps","alternateMeasure":"","scalingMode":"exact"},{"name":"olive oil","quantity":2,"unit":"tbsps","note":"","group":"for the marinade","optional":false,"aisle":"Other","sourceText":"2 tbsps olive oil","sourceQuantity":2,"sourceUnit":"tbsps","alternateMeasure":"","scalingMode":"exact"},{"name":"fresh lemon juice","quantity":2,"unit":"tbsps","note":"","group":"for the marinade","optional":false,"aisle":"Other","sourceText":"2 tbsps fresh lemon juice","sourceQuantity":2,"sourceUnit":"tbsps","alternateMeasure":"","scalingMode":"exact"},{"name":"lemon zest (use an unwaxed lemon), finely grated","quantity":1,"unit":"tbsp","note":"","group":"for the marinade","optional":false,"aisle":"Other","sourceText":"1 tbsp lemon zest (use an unwaxed lemon), finely grated","sourceQuantity":1,"sourceUnit":"tbsp","alternateMeasure":"","scalingMode":"exact"},{"name":"dried rosemary","quantity":1,"unit":"tsp","note":"","group":"for the marinade","optional":false,"aisle":"Other","sourceText":"1 tsp dried rosemary","sourceQuantity":1,"sourceUnit":"tsp","alternateMeasure":"","scalingMode":"exact"},{"name":"dried red chilli flakes","quantity":0.5,"unit":"tsp","note":"","group":"for the marinade","optional":false,"aisle":"Other","sourceText":"½ tsp dried red chilli flakes","sourceQuantity":0.5,"sourceUnit":"tsp","alternateMeasure":"","scalingMode":"exact"},{"name":"dried oregano","quantity":1,"unit":"tsp","note":"","group":"for the marinade","optional":false,"aisle":"Other","sourceText":"1 tsp dried oregano","sourceQuantity":1,"sourceUnit":"tsp","alternateMeasure":"","scalingMode":"exact"},{"name":"dried thyme","quantity":0.5,"unit":"tsp","note":"","group":"for the marinade","optional":false,"aisle":"Other","sourceText":"½ tsp dried thyme","sourceQuantity":0.5,"sourceUnit":"tsp","alternateMeasure":"","scalingMode":"exact"},{"name":"ground black pepper","quantity":0.25,"unit":"tsp","note":"","group":"for the marinade","optional":false,"aisle":"Other","sourceText":"¼ tsp ground black pepper","sourceQuantity":0.25,"sourceUnit":"tsp","alternateMeasure":"","scalingMode":"exact"},{"name":"sea salt","quantity":0.5,"unit":"tsp","note":"","group":"for the marinade","optional":false,"aisle":"Other","sourceText":"½ tsp sea salt","sourceQuantity":0.5,"sourceUnit":"tsp","alternateMeasure":"","scalingMode":"exact"}],"steps":["Take the lamb chops out of the fridge and arrange them in a single layer in a baking dish.","Mix the marinade ingredients in a small bowl. Pour over the chops and spread with a spoon to coat all over.","If cooking soon, leave to marinate at room temperature for 30 minutes. Alternatively, refrigerate for up to 3 hours, then leave at room temperature for 30 minutes before cooking.","Heat a cast-iron frying pan over a medium to high heat. Add the avocado oil or butter and heat for 30 seconds.","Stand the chops on their sides, with the fat against the pan, and fry for 2 minutes.","Lay the chops flat, reduce the heat to medium and fry for 2 to 3 minutes on each side, or until cooked to your liking.","Cover with foil and rest for 2 to 3 minutes before serving.","See Cooking and storage for cooling, storing and reheating leftovers."],"prepMinutes":null,"cookMinutes":null,"waitMinutes":null,"timeNote":"The book does not give separate total preparation, cooking and waiting times. Follow the timings stated in each method step.","notes":"","allergens":[],"allergenNote":"Allergens have not been independen