 cup) cold water","sourceQuantity":120,"sourceUnit":"ml","alternateMeasure":"(½ cup)","scalingMode":"exact"},{"name":"toasted sesame oil","quantity":1,"unit":"tsp","note":"","group":"for the sauce","optional":false,"aisle":"Other","sourceText":"1 tsp toasted sesame oil","sourceQuantity":1,"sourceUnit":"tsp","alternateMeasure":"","scalingMode":"exact"},{"name":"fresh ginger, finely chopped","quantity":2,"unit":"tsps","note":"","group":"for the sauce","optional":false,"aisle":"Other","sourceText":"2 tsps fresh ginger, finely chopped","sourceQuantity":2,"sourceUnit":"tsps","alternateMeasure":"","scalingMode":"exact"},{"name":"fresh garlic, finely chopped","quantity":2,"unit":"tsps","note":"","group":"for the sauce","optional":false,"aisle":"Other","sourceText":"2 tsps fresh garlic, finely chopped","sourceQuantity":2,"sourceUnit":"tsps","alternateMeasure":"","scalingMode":"exact"},{"name":"honey","quantity":1,"unit":"tsp","note":"","group":"for the sauce","optional":false,"aisle":"Other","sourceText":"1 tsp honey","sourceQuantity":1,"sourceUnit":"tsp","alternateMeasure":"","scalingMode":"exact"},{"name":"rice flour or cornflour mixed with 1 tbsp cold water","quantity":1,"unit":"tbsp","note":"","group":"for the sauce","optional":false,"aisle":"Other","sourceText":"1 tbsp rice flour or cornflour mixed with 1 tbsp cold water","sourceQuantity":1,"sourceUnit":"tbsp","alternateMeasure":"","scalingMode":"exact"}],"steps":["Put the soy sauce or tamari, water, garlic, ginger, honey and sesame oil in a saucepan over a medium heat. Stir and simmer for 3 minutes, then increase the heat and bring to the boil.","Reduce the heat to medium. Stir in the rice flour or cornflour mixture and simmer for 2 minutes, or until thickened. Set aside.","Heat 1 tsp coconut oil in a wok over a medium to high heat. Add the broccoli and cook for 4 minutes, stirring frequently.","Season with salt and pepper. Add the pepper and fry for 3 minutes, stirring, then add the mushrooms and fry for 2 to 3 minut